# Keep shell scripts and CI/IaC files LF in every working copy.
#
# core.autocrlf=true is set on at least one Windows machine here, which
# rewrites text files to CRLF on checkout. A CRLF bootstrap.sh is not merely
# untidy -- the shebang line becomes "#!/usr/bin/env bash\r", which Linux
# reads as an interpreter named "bash\r" and refuses to run. These files are
# executed in Cloud Shell and GitHub Actions (both Linux), so they must never
# be checked out with CRLF.
#
# Deliberately NOT applied to *.py: Python reads either line ending, so it buys
# nothing, and it would renormalise ~140 tracked files for no functional gain.
*.sh          text eol=lf
*.sql         text eol=lf
*.yml         text eol=lf
*.yaml        text eol=lf
Dockerfile    text eol=lf
